wolf-lang-packages provides language resource packages as data.

    find_package(wolf-lang-packages CONFIG)

    # A Package search root: one subdirectory per package.
    #   WOLF_LANG_PACKAGES_DIR
    #   WOLF_LANG_PACKAGES_INSTALLED   the suites the selected features brought in

Select suites through features, for example wolf-lang-packages[cmn,jpn]. A suite whose G2P reaches
a shared backend pulls that backend's feature in itself: cmn and yue bring in pinyin, the nine
chain languages bring in multi.

The packages are data. The interpreters that read them ship with wolf, and two of those need a
library of their own at run time: the pinyin backend needs cpp-pinyin, the model backend needs
dsinfer and an ONNX Runtime the host points it at.
